From 757b7eb5a5314e45f8851f993acabc1d18146906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Murphy <christian.murphy.42@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:44:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Match requests with a trie over the route table

Dispatch tried each route in turn, so its cost grew with the table. toHandler and Router.toHandler now build a segment trie once, with RouteIndex.of. A lookup collects the routes whose pattern could match the path. It then runs Route.tryMatch on them in table order.

RouteIndex.matchTable_of proves that the trie picks the route matchTable picks, for every table, method and path. respond?, wantsSlash and slashRedirect? now take a RouteIndex in place of a list of routes.

Signed-off-by: Christian Murphy <christian.murphy.42@gmail.com>
